
  12 synthetic fields of 900 px, 12 cells each
  radius 2.5-8.0 um = 8.8-28.1 px   peak phase 0.8-3.0 rad
  calibration: pitch 0.284871 um, pixel area 0.081151 um^2, 4.300915e-02 pg per rad-pixel
  instance labelling: watershed, watershed distance 15 px

=== pipeline error against exact ground truth ===
  cells placed 144   measured 131   paired 131
  area  signed  mean -0.0289%   median -0.0216%   p95 |.| 0.6078%
  mass  signed  mean -0.0121%   median -0.0062%   p95 |.| 0.1238%
  field-summed mass  mean -2.6733%   median -2.9209%

  13 of 144 cells were never measured. min_cell_area_um2 = 30.0 um^2 rejects anything below 3.09 um of radius,
  and the synthesised radii start at 2.50 um. That is the whole of the gap between a per-cell error of 0.04%
  and a field-summed error of -2.67%: the filter discards small cells, so the
  TOTAL mass of a field is biased low by that much while every cell it keeps is exact.
  Report the filter's cost whenever a field total or a population mean is reported.

